# Dev and test runs only: pixi.toml's [feature.pipeline.activation.env]
# points R_MAKEVARS_USER here. The tree `pixi run build` installs
# (dist/R-*-zig) is the tree that ships, and its Makeconf names the
# environment only as $(R_HOME)/../.. (feat-no-host-paths PLAN.md, F1.5),
# which there is that prefix, not this pixi env. This adds the env's
# headers and libraries, as R installed into a conda env has them in its
# own Makeconf, so packages that link env libraries (data.table's zlib,
# libomp on macOS) compile against the dev tree as they did before.
# CONDA_PREFIX is the activated env (make imports the environment).
# Checks that must see the shipped Makeconf alone run under env -i
# (verify-bundle.sh, hermetic-check.sh) or with R CMD config
# --no-user-files. Windows is told apart by Makeconf's own SHLIB_EXT (R
# reads Makeconf before a user Makevars); OS=Windows_NT does not reach
# make under pixi.
#
# Windows adds LDFLAGS only, as its Makeconf always had (CPPFLAGS stays
# empty there, PLAN.md F1.5): with all of CC, CFLAGS, CXX, CXXFLAGS,
# CPPFLAGS, LDFLAGS, FC and FCFLAGS non-empty in `R CMD config`, R's
# installer, running a configure.win inside another one's (pak builds
# its embedded curl that way), ends with do.call(Sys.setenv, list()):
# "all arguments must be named" (install.R, the configure.win branch).
ifeq ($(SHLIB_EXT),.dll)
LDFLAGS += -L$(subst \,/,$(CONDA_PREFIX))/Library/lib
else
CPPFLAGS += -I$(CONDA_PREFIX)/include
LDFLAGS += -L$(CONDA_PREFIX)/lib -Wl,-rpath,$(CONDA_PREFIX)/lib
endif
